Option J mentions that Euglenas move by flagellum, carry on mixotrophic nutrition, and reproduce asexually through longitudinal binary fission and sporulation. Mixotrophic nutrition means they can both photosynthesize and consume other organic molecules, which aligns with their ability to switch nutrition sources. Binary fission and sporulation are both asexual reproduction methods, so this option is also accurate.

Between options B, F, and J, the most accurate description would be option F, as it correctly identifies the movement mechanism, nutrition capability, and asexual reproduction method. However, option J also provides a correct description, so it's important to consider which option is the best fit.

