The IAIA genotype corresponds to type A blood, and the IAIB genotype corresponds to type B blood. Therefore, the child has a 25% chance of having type A blood and a 75% chance of having type B blood. Since type O blood corresponds to the genotype IAIA, which is not possible in this scenario, the probability of the child having type O blood is 0%.
